cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this codebase or refer to the RELAY method, please cite the
  paper.
title: >
  Learned Relay Representations for Forward-Thinking Discrete Diffusion
  Models
abstract: >
  Masked Diffusion Models (MDMs) generate sequences through iterative
  refinement, but discard the rich internal computation built up over
  masked positions at the end of every denoising step -- the "hard reset"
  problem. We introduce RELAY, which carries the model's last-layer hidden
  states forward as a learned, differentiable relay state and trains it
  end-to-end via truncated backpropagation through time (BPTT). RELAY
  leaves inference-time decoding unchanged, is compatible with block
  diffusion and KV caching, and improves accuracy and inference latency on
  both Sudoku-Extreme and Fast-dLLM v2 1.5B coding benchmarks.
